Changelog: 07-11-2026 20:18:45

Breaking. The window is built as RPCS3 Manager's (owner, 07-11-2026: RPCS3 Manager's design is every manager's). The app
has no Play button any more: a game is started from Steam, and a double-click on a game no longer starts it. Settings…
is gone: Vita3K's settings are in the Settings tab. Covers… is now Steam artwork…, Update Game Mode is now Update Steam,
the Game Mode column is In Steam and the In Game Mode box is Available in Steam. The messages box under the table is
gone: what the app says is in the Log tab.

Changelog: 07-11-2026 20:18:45

Added. The header has the Refresh pill and the boxes, Vita3K version, Firmware, Your games and Available in Steam,
spread over the window's width, with the app's state beside the title. Under the introduction, which links to Vita3K's
release notes and to the wiki, stands a row of action pills: Vita3K Install, Vita3K Uninstall and Games Install, which
opens the menu Install game… had. The state of each follows in three lines, then three tabs: Your games (the table with
Vita3K settings, Remove game…, Steam artwork… and Update Steam, and a link that opens Steam's library), Settings and
Log. What the app says and does goes to its log, ~/.local/share/bc250-vita3k-manager/bc250-vita3k-manager.log (turned
over at 1 MB), shown in the Log tab; install.sh --uninstall keeps it, --purge removes it. The tabs, the pills and the
choice boxes take RPCS3 Manager's style.

Changelog: 07-11-2026 20:18:45

Added. The Vita3K line under the pills says only the state, in the words every manager uses (owner, 07-11-2026): "Not
installed." with "Install it with the Install button." under it, or "Installed." with "Uninstall with the Uninstall
button." under it. The version installed, what Install takes, another version than the app brings, Vita3K updated
itself, and a newer Vita3K are in the line's tooltip; another version and a newer Vita3K also go to the log, once.

