Changelog: 03-11-2026 22:27:51

Release 2.0.0.

Changelog: 03-11-2026 22:09:14

Added. Settings…, a window with Vita3K's settings that matter for playing, in the app (owner, 03-11-2026, from the
Windows Portable Suite's Vita3K Manager; core's settings_page over vita3k_settings): the renderer, the resolution,
the screen filter, anisotropic filtering, fill the screen and VSync; high accuracy, shaders compiled in the
background, the FPS hack, the performance overlay and the shader compilation message; the volume, the sound output
and NGS sound; the confirm button and the PS Vita's language. Each is read from config.yml (build 4186's default
while it names none) and written one line at a time, the rest kept, never while Vita3K runs. The wiki says so.

Changelog: 03-11-2026 21:37:27

Added. Remove game… on Your games (owner, 03-11-2026, from the Windows Portable Suite's managers, 30-10-2026 and
01-11-2026: a game that no longer plays goes, files and all, and before deleting anything the user decides what to
keep; core's keep and keep_dialog): a window lists what of the chosen game would go, a row each with its size, every
row ticked; unticking a row keeps it, Delete marked deletes the rows still ticked off the window's thread (read-only
files too) and takes its Steam shortcut out through Steam when that row is ticked, and Cancel deletes nothing
(library.removal_items(); the saves never among the rows). A game the app will not delete is said so.
The wiki says so.

Changelog: 03-11-2026 21:27:45

Breaking. No file is browsed to for the firmware any more (owner, 03-11-2026, from the Windows Portable Suite's
Vita3K Manager, 30-10-2026: fixed folders, no folder selecting): the button Install firmware…, with its window, is
gone (library.py). Added. The app's own folder: ~/Games/Vita, made with ~/Games/Vita/Firmware when the window
opens, and Games/Vita on each removable drive that has one (mounted under /run/media or /media; core's drives). The
.PUP files put in ~/Games/Vita/Firmware, or in a folder right below it (Sony names all three PSP2UPDAT.PUP), are
given to Vita3K by itself, the largest first, one after the other, once Vita3K is installed, when the window opens
and on Refresh, while Vita3K does not run (sync_firmware(), library.firmware_files()); each file is given once while
it stays the same (its place, size and time in the settings, firmware_given), one Vita3K could not use too, and a
file replaced is given again. The files stay. The Firmware line says where to put them while the firmware is
missing, and the output names each file given. Install game…'s windows open in ~/Games/Vita. The wiki says so.

Changelog: 03-11-2026 21:04:45

Fixed. Update Steam reads Steam's file back right after writing it, while Steam is still closed, and says on the
status line and in the output when a game it wrote is not found there, by name (owner, 03-11-2026, from the Windows
Portable Suite's managers, 29-10-2026: "it still says 0 games in Steam"), so the message tells whether the file or
the reading is at fault; a failed read of the file is said too instead of passed over. Nothing changes when the
shortcuts read back as written.

Changelog: 03-11-2026 20:54:32

Fixed. No user name on the screen or in the log (owner, 03-11-2026: the suite's privacy rule, as the Windows Portable
Suite's apps keep it since 29-10-2026): Vita3K's storage on the firmware and games steps, and every message under the tabs and in the output show your home folder as ~ (core's platform.private).

Changelog: 03-11-2026 20:51:07

Added. The app turns Vita3K's welcome window and its own update check off in config.yml (show-welcome false,
check-for-updates-mode 0), once Vita3K is installed, each time the window opens and never while Vita3K runs, since
it writes its settings back when it closes (owner, 03-11-2026, from the Windows Portable Suite's Vita3K Manager): the
welcome window would wait for a click before a game, and the update check would offer a build the app was not tried
with. The app wrote nothing in config.yml before. Every other line stays as Vita3K wrote it; the window's output says
what changed (userdata.set_values(), prepare(), emulator.running()). The wiki says so.

