Release 0.6.0.

Changelog: 22-10-2026 18:09:01

Added. Covers from SteamGridDB for the portrait in Steam's library (owner, 22-10-2026). A PS Vita game has no 2:3
picture of its own, so the portrait was always drawn from its icon and title. With the suite's SteamGridDB API key,
one for every app (core's covers, kept in ~/.config/bc250-bazzite-suite/steamgriddb-key) and entered under the new
Covers… button, Update Game Mode first looks each ticked game up by its title and takes the still 600 × 900
portrait with the highest score, leaving out those marked nsfw, humor or epilepsy. Only the portrait: the wide
picture, the banner and the logo stay the game's own icon and LiveArea picture. What is found is kept in
~/.local/share/bc250-vita3k-manager/covers under the game's title ID, and a game looked up is not asked for again; a
game in Steam not yet looked up turns Update Game Mode on. A refused key or no network stops the lookup with a
message and the drawn portrait is used; the shortcuts are written all the same. Without a key nothing changes. The
artwork is now drawn in the background job, after the lookup. install.sh --uninstall --purge removes the covers folder too; the installer test checks it. Test: the pictures found in place of the drawn
portrait, and Covers… with Update Game Mode in the window, with SteamGridDB's answers made in the test.

